{number: 26}
{title: O Little Town of Bethlehem}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] O little town of [F] Bethlehem,
How [C] still we [G7] see thee [C] lie!
Above thy [A7] deep and [Dm] dreamless sleep
The [C] silent [G7] stars go [C] by;
Yet [C] in thy dark streets [Am] shin-[B7] eth
The [Em] everlasting [G] Light;
The [C] hopes and fears of [F] all the years
Are [C] met in [G7] thee to-[C] night.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
For [C] Christ is born of [F] Mary;
And [C] gathered [G7] all a-[C] bove,
While [A7] mortals sleep, the [Dm] angels keep
Their [C] watch of [G7] wond'ring [C] love,
O [C] morning stars, to-[Am] geth-[B7] er
Pro-[Em] claim the holy [G] birth!
And [C] praises sing to [F] God the King,
And [C] peace to [G7] men on [C] earth.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
How [C] silently, how [F] silently,
The [C] wondrous [G7] gift is [C] giv'n!
So [A7] God imparts to [Dm] human hearts
The [C] blessings [G7] of His [C] Heav'n.
No [C] ear may hear His [Am] com-[B7] ing;
But [Em] in this world of [G] sin,
Where [C] meek souls will re-[F] ceive Him still,
The [C] dear Christ [G7] enters [C] in.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
O [C] holy Child of [F] Bethlehem,
De-[C] scend to [G7] us, we [C] pray;
Cast [A7] out our sin, and [Dm] enter in,
Be [C] born in [G7] us to-[C] day.
We [C] hear the Christmas [Am] an-[B7] gels
The [Em] great glad tidings [G] tell,--
O [C] come to us, a-[F] bide with us,
Our [C] Lord Em-[G7] manu-[C] el.
{end_of_verse}
